{"data": {"notes": [], "reqs": [{"kind": "contract", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R1", "source": {"type": "task_metadata"}, "status": "active", "text": "Entry point `solve` in language python, within the stated limits.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "hard", "requirement_id": "R2", "source": {"char_end": 1665, "char_start": 0, "quote": "You are an expert Python programmer. You will be given a question (problem specification) and will generate a correct Python program that matches the specification and passes all tests.\n\n### Question:\nYou are given a sequence of M integers A = (A_1, A_2, \\dots, A_M).\nEach element of A is an integer between 1 and N, inclusive, and all elements are distinct.\nList all integers between 1 and N that do not appear in A in ascending order.\n\nInput\n\nThe input is given from Standard Input in the following format:\nN M\nA_1 A_2 \\dots A_M\n\nOutput\n\nLet (X_1, X_2, \\dots, X_C) be the sequence of all integers between 1 and N, inclusive, that do not appear in A, listed in ascending order.\nThe output should be in the following format:\nC\nX_1 X_2 \\dots X_C\n\nConstraints\n\n\n- All input values are integers.\n- 1 \\le M \\le N \\le 1000\n- 1 \\le A_i \\le N\n- The elements of A are distinct.\n\nSample Input 1\n\n10 3\n3 9 2\n\nSample Output 1\n\n7\n1 4 5 6 7 8 10\n\nHere, A=(3,9,2).\nThe integers between 1 and 10 that do not appear in A, listed in ascending order, are 1,4,5,6,7,8,10.\n\nSample Input 2\n\n6 6\n1 3 5 2 4 6\n\nSample Output 2\n\n0\n\n\nNo integer between 1 and 6 is missing from A.\nIn this case, print 0 on the first line and leave the second line empty.\n\nSample Input 3\n\n9 1\n9\n\nSample Output 3\n\n8\n1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8\n\n### Format: Read the inputs from stdin solve the problem and write the answer to stdout (do not directly test on the sample inputs). Enclose your code within delimiters as follows. Ensure that when the python program runs, it reads the inputs, runs the algorithm and writes output to STDOUT.\n```python\n# YOUR CODE HERE\n```\n\n### Answer: (use the provided format with backticks)\n\n", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "The program is correct on all legal inputs of the statement.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R3", "source": {"char_end": 1719, "char_start": 1677, "quote": "Input:\n10 3\n3 9 2\nOutput:\n7\n1 4 5 6 7 8 10", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 1: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R4", "source": {"char_end": 1763, "char_start": 1731, "quote": "Input:\n6 6\n1 3 5 2 4 6\nOutput:\n0", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 2: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}, {"kind": "explicit", "priority": "functional", "requirement_id": "R5", "source": {"char_end": 1813, "char_start": 1775, "quote": "Input:\n9 1\n9\nOutput:\n8\n1 2 3 4 5 6 7 8", "type": "request_span"}, "status": "active", "text": "Public example 3: output exactly the quoted output for the quoted input.", "version": 1}], "request_sha": "4a1caa38798edfc6471d13bf6d6fa0dfeba63cb8c65e85fd0e48ba6fdf4986f6", "stop": null}, "kind": "requirements", "prev": "70612090f093058939d99517b55c1b5fcbdf84e9d97c810ffd1415fb94c71101", "seq": 2}
